#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1178
#, kde-format
msgid "Crop left"
msgstr "Recortar pola esquerda"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1180
#, fuzzy, kde-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<![CDATA[Crops data from the left side of the graph (effectively zooming "
#| "in). <br>\n"
#| "    \tThe value is interpreted either as a percentage of total or an "
#| "absolute value depending on crop_mode_h. In percentage mode, the values "
#| "are not restricted to 0-100 to allow for \"zoom out\" behaviour (ie: "
#| "cropping -50 left will add an extra half of the total horizontal "
#| "distance). Values over 100 (in % mode) will effectively not display "
#| "anything. If <em>Graph Type</em> is set to <b>Speedometer</b>, all crop "
#| "left/right values are ignored.]]>"
msgid ""
"Crops data from the left side of the graph (effectively zooming in). <br>\n"
"    \tThe value is interpreted either as a percentage of total or an "
"absolute value depending on crop_mode_h. In percentage mode, the values are "
"not restricted to 0-100 to allow for \"zoom out\" behaviour (ie: cropping "
"-50 left will add an extra half of the total horizontal distance). Values "
"over 100 (in % mode) will effectively not display anything. If <em>Graph "
"Type</em> is set to <b>Speedometer</b>, all crop left/right values are "
"ignored."
msgstr ""
"<![CDATA[Recorta datos do lado esquerdo da gráfica (co efecto de ampliar). "
"<br>\n"
"    \tO valor interprétase ou como unha porcentaxe do total ou como valor "
"absoluto segundo crop_mode_h. No modo de porcentaxe, os valores non están "
"restrinxidos a 0-100 para permitir o comportamento de «afastar» (é dicir, "
"recortar -50 da esquerda engade unha metade adicional da distancia total do "
"horizonte). Os valores por riba de 100 (no modo %) resultarán en non amosar "
"nada. Se o <em>tipo de gráfico</em> está definido como <b>Velocímetro</b>, "
"os valores de recorte de esquerda e dereita ignóranse.]]>"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1182
#, kde-format
msgid "Crop right"
msgstr "Recortar pola dereita"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1184
#, fuzzy, kde-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<![CDATA[Same as <em>Crop left</em> but for the right side, and "
#| "percentage type is interpreted as an inverse percentage (ie: 100 = do not "
#| "crop anything). Values under 0 will effectively not display anything.]]>"
msgid ""
"Same as <em>Crop left</em> but for the right side, and percentage type is "
"interpreted as an inverse percentage (ie: 100 = do not crop anything). "
"Values under 0 will effectively not display anything."
msgstr ""
"<![CDATA[Igual que <em>Recortar pola esquerda</em> pero pola dereita, e o "
"tipo de porcentaxe interprétase como unha porcentaxe inversa (é dicir, 100 "
"non recorta nada). Os valores inferiores a 0 resultarán en que non se amose "
"nada.]]>"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1186
#, kde-format
msgid "Crop mode vertical"
msgstr "Modo de recorte vertical"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1188
#, fuzzy, kde-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<![CDATA[Decides how to interpret the <em>Crop bottom</em> and <em>Crop "
#| "top</em> values.<br/>\n"
#| "    \tWith an absolute value, it can zoom in to between 100 and 150m of "
#| "altitude to show\n"
#| "small changes in altitude between those 2 values better.<br/>\n"
#| "Note: for the vertical type, absolute values are latitude degrees (for "
#| "the location\n"
#| "source type) and altitude, heart rate, speed for the others interpreted "
#| "as the <em>Legend unit</em>\n"
#| "type where applicable (ie: a value of 10 for altitude will be considered "
#| "meters by default\n"
#| "but if changing <em>Legend unit</em> to feet it will mean 10 feet).]]>"
msgid ""
"Decides how to interpret the <em>Crop bottom</em> and <em>Crop top</em> "
"values.<br/>\n"
"    \tWith an absolute value, it can zoom in to between 100 and 150m of "
"altitude to show\n"
"small changes in altitude between those 2 values better.<br/>\n"
"Note: for the vertical type, absolute values are latitude degrees (for the "
"location\n"
"source type) and altitude, heart rate, speed for the others interpreted as "
"the <em>Legend unit</em>\n"
"type where applicable (ie: a value of 10 for altitude will be considered "
"meters by default\n"
"but if changing <em>Legend unit</em> to feet it will mean 10 feet)."
msgstr ""
"<![CDATA[Determina como interpretar os valores de <em>Recortar por abaixo</"
"em> e <em>Recortar por arriba</em>.<br/>\n"
"    \tCun valor absoluto, pode ampliar a entre 100 e 150 metros de altitude "
"para amosar\n"
"mellor pequenos cambios de altitude entre eses 2 valores.<br/>\n"
"Nota: Para o tipo vertical, os valores absolutos son graos de latitude (para "
"o tipo de fonte\n"
"da localización) e de altitude, frecuencia cardíaca e velocidade. O resto "
"interprétanse como\n"
"o tipo de <em>Unidade da lenda</em> onde sexa aplicábel (é dicir, un valor "
"de 10 para a\n"
"altitude considerarase en metros de maneira predeterminada, pero se cambia "
"a\n"
"<em>Unidade da lenda</em> a pés, significará 10 pés.]]>"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1192
#, kde-format
msgid "Crop bottom"
msgstr "Recortar por abaixo"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1194
#, fuzzy, kde-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<![CDATA[Crops data from the bottom side of the graph (effectively "
#| "zooming in). <br>\n"
#| "    \tThe value is interpreted either as a percentage of total or an "
#| "absolute value depending on crop_mode_v. In percentage mode the values "
#| "are not restricted to 0-100 to allow for \"zoom out\" behaviour (ie: "
#| "cropping -50 bot will add an extra half of the total vertical distance to "
#| "the bottom). Values over 100 (in % mode) will effectively not display "
#| "anything. If <em>Graph type</em> is <b>Speedometer</b>, this will set the "
#| "minimum needle position which will clamp all values that are lower.]]>"
msgid ""
"Crops data from the bottom side of the graph (effectively zooming in). <br>\n"
"    \tThe value is interpreted either as a percentage of total or an "
"absolute value depending on crop_mode_v. In percentage mode the values are "
"not restricted to 0-100 to allow for \"zoom out\" behaviour (ie: cropping "
"-50 bot will add an extra half of the total vertical distance to the "
"bottom). Values over 100 (in % mode) will effectively not display anything. "
"If <em>Graph type</em> is <b>Speedometer</b>, this will set the minimum "
"needle position which will clamp all values that are lower."
msgstr ""
"<![CDATA[Recorta datos da parte inferior do gráfico (co efecto de ampliar). "
"<br>\n"
"    \tO valor interprétase como porcentaxe do total ou como valor absoluto "
"segundo crop_mode_v. No modo de porcentaxe os valores non están restrinxidos "
"a 0-100 para permitir o comportamento de «afastar» (é dicir, recortar -50 "
"engade unha metade adicional á distancia vertical total inferior). Os "
"valores por riba de 100 (no modo %) farán que non se vexa nada. Se o "
"<em>tipo de gráfico</em> é <b>Velocímetro</b>, isto definirá a posición "
"mínima da agulla, o que recortará todos os valores inferiores.]]>"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
